knights and questing name a more iconic  duo  whenever you think of the medieval age  it's a partnership that often springs to  mind  in which knights would undertake daring  quests to save a damsel retrieve a holy  artifact or capture a castle  but did this sort of thing actually  happen did medieval knights really go  questing  so the answer for the most part is no  sorry the notion of a knight wandering  into a tavern and getting a quest or his  king asking him to find a holy relic  just wasn't a thing  we'll focus on the late medieval period  since this was peak chivalry  most knights were of middling rank who  served a local lord and they spent most  of their time  administering their own lands making  sure your peasants paid you you  fulfilled your obligations to your lord  and maintaining law and order was a  full-time job  which as you'll note isn't questing  knights were also responsible for some  military duties like providing levies  and they themselves were expected to  stay in top form which sometimes  included traveling to tournaments  so the knights that administered land  often had several sons and only one of  them was going to inherit it all  so what about the rest well they mostly  caused trouble  some though would stay in their family  territories and were responsible for  things like collecting tolls  you see traveling across medieval europe  could be dangerous and it's often  because of these tolls  knights and lords would demand payment  for safe passage through their lands and  if you couldn't pay you'd be forced out  and if you didn't pay but sort of looked  like you could you were liable for being  ransomed  often these wayward sons and their  friends would join mercenary bands to  fight all over europe and often on  behalf of the lord they would raid their  neighbours  and all of this was illegal and so many  young knights and even high-ranking  noblemen were imprisoned and punished  for doing it  in fact 15th century france and the holy  roman empire had a real problem with  robber knights  who as the name suggests were knights  who just went around and robbed people  these were particularly bad during  periods of national instability  if central authority was diminished  knights would just go to town  and then robert blind so was there  anything similar to our idea of  requesting night  the only other real example of questing  in the traditional spiritual sense of  accomplishing a great feat  is the crusades knights and lords of all  inheritances would answer the pope's  call and travel to the holy land to do  their christian duty and retake some  cities and safeguards and artifacts  the call to crusade was one of the  spiritual quest as well as one for luton  prestige  but barring that the idea of a knight or  a small group of adventurers setting out  on a quest for an item or something  along those lines  just didn't happen except in literature  i hope you enjoyed this episode and  thank you for watching with a special  thanks to my patrons james bisonette  kelly money maker the pastry section  marvin cassow rob waterhouse danny  maloney  moe aaron the white james castaneda  jordan longley marcus asner jerry lamdin  gustav swan rasheed ali  colin carson copper tone izzy david  silverman spinning three plates  winston k wood spencer lightfoot maggie  paxkowski  matthew shipley anthony beckett  fortunate calf robert wetzel lexi  schwinn and skye chappelle
 

